    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203462": {
      "title": "Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track & Field (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track & Field (Part-Time) Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track & Field (Part-Time) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track & Field (Part-Time) Category: Staff  Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Administration, Strategic Initiatives, Trustee Affairs-Athletics Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Aug 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 203462 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: The Assistant Track & Field Coach is responsible for assisting both programs in all aspects of administration and operation of a competitive Division I collegiate track and field and cross-country program.  Duties include: Aid with practice/competition activities for an NCAA Division I program; Help manage student-athlete skill development and performance analysis; Abide by and comply with National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA), Conference rules, academic standards, requirements, and policies of the Department of Athletics and University; Interact with a wide variety of people in a manner that positively portrays the University, its programs, and its personnel; Promote a culture of inclusion, working effectively within a culture of individuals with diverse backgrounds, styles, abilities, and motivations; Contribute to the overall success of the university's intercollegiate athletics program by performing all other duties and responsibilities as assigned; Work is performed in an indoor/outdoor environment. Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Requirements: Must have a bachelor's degree or higher 1 - 2 years of collegiate or professional coaching or playing experience Knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations. Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. URL: BUKnights.com Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
    },
    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204506": {
      "title": "Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director, Athletic Communication",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Assistant Director, Athletic Communication Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director, Athletic Communication Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director, Athletic Communication Category: Staff  Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Administration, Strategic Initiatives, Trustee Affairs-Athletics Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Sep 4, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 204506 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: This is a professional position responsible for assisting the Assistant A.D. for Athletics Communication with all facets of athletic communication, including game-day operations, media relations, social media content, video/broadcast productions, publications, and photography. Specific responsibilities include: Oversee the staffing and production of webcasts and broadcast productions. Serve as the primary media contact for assigned teams, including recruiting appropriate game day staff where applicable. Report statistics to NCAA and conference offices. Work with coaches to nominate and promote student-athletes and athletic personnel for appropriate awards and recognitions. Assist in maintaining media archives (photos, videos, etc.) as well as statistical records. Oversee the performance of student workers. Assist the Assistant Athletics Director for Athletics Communication in the day-to-day administrative duties. Assist the athletics department with operational duties assigned by the Director of Athletics or his/her designee. Requirements: Bachelor's Degree required Work experience in journalism, broadcasting, or athletic administration Ability to visually analyze live athletic competitions. Possess a willingness and ability to support and promote a diverse and inclusive campus community Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. URL: BUKnights.com Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
