    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200525": {
      "title": "Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Supervisor, Campus Event Operations (Utility Team)",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Assistant Supervisor, Campus Event Operations (Utility Team) Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Supervisor, Campus Event Operations (Utility Team) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Supervisor, Campus Event Operations (Utility Team) Category: Staff  Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Finance-Facilities Management Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: May 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 200525 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: The Assistant Supervisor, Campus Event Operations (Utility Team) will be responsible for overseeing the university's utility team in the Supervisor's absence.  This position ensures timely and efficient completion of special setups for numerous campus functions, moving of equipment and furniture and completion of all assigned work orders. Requirements: Supervisory Responsibilities: Coordinate with the Utility Team Supervisor and Office of Facilities Management to oversee the daily workflow. Partner with leadership to identify talent gaps, assign work orders, and maintain weekly U-Team schedules. Ensure the proper, safe, and efficient use of materials, equipment, and vehicles belonging to the University U-Team Department. Demonstrate proper safety and procedures in campus set-ups and furniture and equipment moves. Performs other related duties as assigned. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Ensure the timely and efficient completion of special setups for the numerous campus functions, moving of equipment and furniture, and the proper completion of all assigned work orders. Perform all assigned setups and moves, as well as all other assigned tasks, under the direction of the U-Team Supervisor. Ensure the proper and efficient use and maintenance of all issued materials, tools, and equipment belonging to the university. During winter months, sweep snow and ice from doorways, sidewalks, and pathways next to assigned buildings, and other areas where assistance in snow and ice removal is needed. Perform construction cleanup or demolition as needed. Ensure that assigned University vehicles are kept clean, and all maintenance problems are properly reported. Report all maintenance-related items to supervisor. Perform all other duties as assigned by supervisory staff, within the scope of this job description, and individual training and experience. Have the flexibility to work in areas outside your assigned areas of responsibility, as directed by the supervisor.  Individuals may be assigned duties in Maintenance or Grounds on a temporary basis. Interpersonal and Professional Skills: Be able to work and interact positively within a diverse, multi-cultural environment, and communicate with all members of the campus community in a professional and respectful manner. Required Education and Experience: A High School education, or equivalent (GED), is requested. However, the education requirement may be substituted by work experience, at the discretion of the Director of Facilities Management. However, the applicant must have either a High School equivalent education or at least 6 months of previous work experience. Applicant must possess the ability to learn new skills as required and be able to work with minimal or no supervision, individually or in a team setting. Applicant must possess a valid driver's license and have an MVR that passes the criteria set by our insurance carriers. Applicant must possess a willingness to learn and the ability to perform the physical demands of the position. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in a similar role is preferred. Physical Demands and Working Conditions: Exposure to potentially hazardous materials is possible.  Occasionally, you may need to handle and transport items weighing more than 50 pounds. Must be comfortable working at heights above twelve feet and performing minor electrical repairs. Disclaimer: This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive. The employee may perform other related duties assigned to meet the organization's ongoing needs. Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
    },
    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204510": {
      "title": "Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Director of Game Operations & Ticketing",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Director of Game Operations & Ticketing Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Director of Game Operations & Ticketing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Game Operations & Ticketing Category: Staff  Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Administration, Strategic Initiatives, Trustee Affairs-Athletics Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Sep 4, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 204510 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: This is a professional position responsible for assisting the Senior Associate A.D. for Facility & Event Management with all phases of game-day operations. Specific responsibilities include: Support ticketing operations for the department of athletics, including season tickets for volleyball, wrestling, and women's & men's basketball.  Create ticketing initiatives and promotions to drive attendance at non-revenue sports. Assist in game-day operations for various sports, including event setup/break down, safety/security, housekeeping, visiting team and officials hospitality, and other duties.  Aid in various special events as needed. Assist the Senior Associate A.D. for Facility & Event Management in athletic-related rentals of athletic facilities, including contract formation, representing the department at day-of-event, and billing reconciliation. Work with on-campus partners when university events require athletic facilities for events that support the university's mission. Ensure that all events overseen meet Bellarmine, NCAA, and conference standards and expectations. Assist in maintaining and upkeep of athletic facilities to ensure they are up to safety standards and expectations. Develop and maintain emergency action plans for all athletic facilities. Assist the Senior Associate A.D. for Facility & Event Management in the day-to-day administrative duties. Assist the athletics department with operational duties assigned by the Director of Athletics or his/her designee. Requirements: Bachelor's Degree required Experience in a collegiate athletic environment. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, verbal, and written skills. Possess a willingness and ability to support and promote a diverse and inclusive campus community Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. URL: BUKnights.com Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
    },
    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=190851": {
      "title": "Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: General Groundsperson",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: General Groundsperson Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: General Groundsperson Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details General Groundsperson Category: Staff  Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Finance-Facilities Management Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Jul 24, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 190851 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: This is a regular, full-time position with normal working hours. Number of months per year is 12. Occasionally may work additional hours to clear snow and ice from roads and sidewalks and perform weekend cleanup/setup for special Bellarmine functions. May be called in during emergencies. When working additional hours, will receive overtime pay as appropriate. Perform tasks as assigned by the Grounds Supervisor relating to plant beds, turf maintenance, athletics field preparation, trash, leaf and snow removal, etc. Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Requirements: Essential Responsibilities: Operate equipment necessary for maintaining the University grounds. Aid in keeping equipment clean and operable and maintain the shop area. Ensure the proper, safe and efficient use of materials, equipment, and vehicles belonging to the University Grounds Department. Perform snow removal under the direction of the Ground Supervisor. During periods when no grounds work can be performed, maintain and perform PM maintenance on Grounds equipment. Perform other duties as assigned by the Grounds Supervisor. Must be able to work and interact positively within a diverse, multi-cultural environment, and communicate with all members of the campus community in a professional and respectful manner. Must be able to work professionally both individually and in a team setting. Additional Information: Secondary Responsibilities: Be temporarily assigned to other Facilities Management areas as needed. Minimum Qualifications for Consideration: Knowledge of lawn maintenance equipment and ability to operate lawn mowers, string trimmers, etc. Applicant must possess a valid driver's license and have an MVR that passes the criteria set by our insurance carriers. Working Conditions Exposure to potentially hazardous chemicals and grounds maintenance equipment.  Exposure to extreme weather conditions, allergens, plant poisons, and insects. Occasionally may need to lift and transport items weighing up to 50 pounds. Application Instructions: Please submit a resume, cover letter (not required) and contact information for three professional references. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
